# memory/index is exempt from the missing-index rule

The other carve-out, and a different one from `generated-index-exempt`: that
case exempts a file from the filename rule, this one exempts a directory from
the missing-index rule. `memory/index` has a child directory and no
`memory/index/memory.md`, which the second rejection path would otherwise
condemn.

The payload is named `memory.md` on purpose, so this case rests on the
`memory|memory/index` arm alone and not on the filename carve-out.
